From: ETNA <etna@example.com>
Date: Fri, 1 May 2026 23:57:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix deBruijn graphs (synthesised from upstream 8e1591a1)

Upstream fix: 8e1591a1d4ad435f766dac4672da66d733816293
"Fix deBruijn graphs"

The buggy code returned @vertex []@ for the dimension-0 De Bruijn graph,
but every other case in the deBruijn family is a graph with /A^(D+1)/
edges. Dimension 0 should be a single self-loop on the empty word,
i.e. @edge [] []@. With @vertex []@, the graph has 0 edges instead of 1.

The forward direction of this patch IS the upstream fix (-buggy → +fixed),
matching git-format-patch convention. Base tree already contains the fix;
`git apply -R` reinstates the bug.
---
 src/Algebra/Graph.hs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Algebra/Graph.hs b/src/Algebra/Graph.hs
--- a/src/Algebra/Graph.hs
+++ b/src/Algebra/Graph.hs
@@ -1029,7 +1029,7 @@
 -- n > 0 ==> 'edgeCount'   (deBruijn n xs) == ('length' $ 'Data.List.nub' xs)^(n + 1)
 -- @
 deBruijn :: Int -> [a] -> Graph [a]
-deBruijn 0   _        = vertex []
+deBruijn 0   _        = edge [] []
 deBruijn len alphabet = skeleton >>= expand
   where
     overlaps = mapM (const alphabet) [2..len]
